{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 125, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a skip where edge 3 was empty restores the residual path, giving gains up to +45 on IN16 (exps 7, 11, 12), versus small gains when it replaces an existing op (exps 8-10)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty input-to-output edge with a 3x3 conv creates a new path and gives large gains (exps 58-62), while replacing an existing op there gives less."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without the direct edge 3 shortcut, a skip on edge 0 supplies residual flow (+12.6 IN16, exp 44 vs +0.53, exp 38)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "A skip on edge 1 partly substitutes for the missing input-to-output shortcut (+10.2 IN16, exp 45 vs +0.33, exp 39)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "A skip into the output node helps far more when edge 3 provides no shortcut (exp 47 vs exp 41)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a conv on edge 5 with a skip adds needed identity flow when edge 3 is missing (exp 48 vs exp 42)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a third path into the output matters more when edge 3 is absent (exp 4: +4.68 C100 vs exps 1 and 5)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 1 already removed, deleting edge 0 cuts every path through the intermediate nodes and can nearly disconnect the cell (exp 17, about -78 on C10)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing a 3x3 conv on the direct edge loses a strong path (-11.27 IN16, exp 69), whereas the edit does nothing or little when edge 3 holds a weaker or empty op."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting a 3x3 conv on the final edge into the output consistently hurts (exps 63-66), whereas the edit is neutral when edge 5 is already none."}], "tok": 32127, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [0, "none"]], [["nor_co